{"term":"spawn","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a72fef445361d78f5d","definition":"To produce or deposit (eggs) in water.","example":"A frog spawns thousands of tadpoles every year.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["despawn","spawnable","spawner","spawny","unspawned","respawn"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eb8e6fc1e4e7c4b6c2","definition":"To generate, bring into being, especially nonmammalian beings in very large numbers.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["despawn","spawnable","spawner","spawny","unspawned","respawn"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:94e10b4b4c91d87453","definition":"To bring forth in general.","example":"The web server spawns a new process to handle each client's request.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["despawn","spawnable","spawner","spawny","unspawned","respawn"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aa319cf8704c1033ec","definition":"To induce (aquatic organisms) to spawn.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["despawn","spawnable","spawner","spawny","unspawned","respawn"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spawn#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:56a8e0